# [Compare launch commands]($heading.id('choose-a-decoding-mode'))

Run one command at a time. Each example uses the default batch size,
context length, and sampling settings.

```=html
<div class="cli-decoding-comparison">
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">Standard · Shell</span>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy standard decoding command">llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3-4B</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">Native MTP · Shell</span>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy native MTP command">llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next \
  --speculative-drafter-model=native</code></pre>
  </div>
  <div class="command-shell">
    <span class="command-language">External drafter · Shell</span>
    <pre><code class="sh" data-copy-label="Copy external drafter command">llmd --model=hf://Qwen/Qwen3-4B \
  --speculative-drafter-model=hf://deepseek-ai/dspark_qwen3_4b_block7</code></pre>
  </div>
</div>
```

Standard decoding takes only the target model. Native multi-token prediction
(MTP) uses the target's own drafter, as shown with `Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next`.
The external example loads a compatible target and drafter from Hugging Face at launch.
See [Model compatibility]($link.page('llmd/reference/model-compatibility')) for other models and modes.

# [Sampling controls and precedence]($heading.id('sampling-and-speculative-decoding'))

The [LLMD 20261112.0 release](https://zml.ai/posts/llmd-20261112.0/#sampling-controls)
documents these controls. Check the options exposed by your installed build.

| LLMD option | CLI default or fallback | Highest priority first | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `--top-k=<number>` | Unset, fallback `50` | CLI → model → fallback | Limit sampling to the highest-ranked tokens. |
| `--top-p=<fraction>` | Unset, fallback `1.0` | Chat request → CLI → model → fallback | Keep tokens within a cumulative probability threshold. Accepted values are `0` through `1`. |
| `--min-p=<fraction>` | Unset, fallback `0.0` | CLI → model → fallback | Set a minimum probability threshold relative to the most probable token. Accepted values are `0` through `1`. |
| `--temperature=<number>` | Unset, fallback `1.0` | Chat request → CLI → model → fallback | Scale the sampling distribution. |

# [Speculative decoding flags]($heading.id('speculative-decoding-flags'))

| LLMD option | Default | Effect |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `--speculative-drafter-model=<path>` | Unset | Enable speculative decoding with a compatible drafter model or `native` where supported. |
| `--speculative-draft-count=<tokens>` | Derived from the model configuration | Override the number of draft tokens to verify. |

# [External drafter options]($heading.id('external-drafter-options'))

Select the exact model, backend, and drafter under
[External drafters]($link.page('llmd/reference/model-compatibility').unsafeRef('external-drafters')),
then choose **Configure launch**. External pairings use LLMD's defaults unless
you supply an override or select a preset with its own settings.
Omit `--speculative-draft-count` to use the count derived from the model
configuration.

> # [Use locally downloaded weights]($block.collapsible(false).attrs('client-disclosure'))
>
> Download both repositories under `${HOME}/models`. Pass each host directory
> to a native installation. See
> [Local model files]($link.page('llmd/howto/model-storage').ref('local'))
> for directory contents and revision options.
>
> ```sh
> llmd --model="${HOME}/models/Qwen/Qwen3-4B" \
>   --speculative-drafter-model="${HOME}/models/deepseek-ai/dspark_qwen3_4b_block7"
> ```
>
> On a CUDA Docker host, mount both directories read-only and pass their
> container paths to LLMD.
>
> ```sh
> docker run --rm --gpus=all --shm-size=256GB -p 127.0.0.1:8000:8000 \
>   --mount "type=bind,source=${HOME}/models/Qwen/Qwen3-4B,target=/model,readonly" \
>   --mount "type=bind,source=${HOME}/models/deepseek-ai/dspark_qwen3_4b_block7,target=/drafter,readonly" \
>   zmlai/llmd:cuda --model=/model --speculative-drafter-model=/drafter
> ```

> # [Published DSpine preset override]($block.collapsible(false).attrs('client-disclosure'))
>
> The published Qwen3.8-27B recipe pairs the model with
> `tencent/Qwen3.8-27B-DSpine-b16` and sets `--batch-size=1` on both
> [CUDA]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/start').unsafeRef('qwen3-8-27b-cuda-dspine'))
> and [ROCm]($link.page('llmd/tutorial/start').unsafeRef('qwen3-8-27b-rocm-dspine')).
